WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/HealthRecommendations.tsx — a presentational leaf
  fed { overallHealth: 'good' | 'warning' | 'critical' } by the Drivetrain Health page.
  Data hooks: useTranslation only (the parent owns the query lifecycle).
  It renders <FadeIn delay={0.35}><GlassPanel p-6>:
    • header  : <Shield class="text-neon-cyan"/> + <h3 uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--text-muted)]>
                {t('drivetrain.recommendations','Health Recommendations')}
    • list    : a useMemo([overallHealth, t]) of tips rendered in a <StaggerContainer> of <StaggerItem> cards,
                each "flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3" with a priority-driven border + fill
                and a leading glyph, over <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">{tip.text}</p>.
  The recommendation memo (reproduced VERBATIM — same conditionals, same push order):
    1. overallHealth === 'critical'                         → criticalStop, serviceUrgent          (priority high)
    2. overallHealth === 'warning' OR 'critical'            → reduceLoad, checkCoolant, avoidSupercharging (medium)
    3. always                                               → regularService, gentleAccel, precondition,
                                                              monitorTemps                          (priority low)
  ⇒ good = 4 tips · warning = 7 tips · critical = 9 tips. The list is never empty.
  Priority styling : high → text-neon-red + AlertTriangle + border-neon-red/20 + bg-neon-red/5;
                     medium → text-neon-amber + AlertTriangle + border-neon-amber/20 + bg-neon-amber/5;
                     low  → text-neon-cyan + TrendingUp + border-[var(--border-subtle)] + bg-white/[0.02].

