WHY-DEFERRED (full-app xcodebuild RED is NOT this surface)
  • iOS  : the whole app target — which includes HealthRecommendations.* — BUILD SUCCEEDED. The failure is in
           the single aggregated XCTest bundle (TeslaSyncTests), into which EVERY co-located *Tests.swift is
           compiled; ~300 surfaces collide there on duplicate XCTestCase / spy type names and a handful of
           pre-existing non-Sendable test closures. None of the 14 errors is in HealthRecommendations, whose
           test types are uniquely prefixed (HealthRecommendations{Projector,Model,Accessibility,ViewState}Tests,
           SpyHealthRecommendationsTelemetry). Proof: those same 28 tests compile + pass in the isolated bundle [5].
  • macOS: development-signing required for the app + widget entitlements; no dev certificate on this runner.
  Both are the architecture-wide conditions owned by the p4-apple/P99-0001 acceptance gate on a signed
  macos-latest runner (apps/macos-pending-verifications.md) — the same DEFERRED disposition every prior P4
  surface ships under (ColorConverter, HealthOverview, HealthGaugeGrid, …). This commit is purely additive and
  neither introduces nor touches any failing file.

